From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: glacier <hyouga.dev@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 12 Oct 2026 19:32:20 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] Check what players report against what they could have done

Server-authoritative checks (AthenaGuard), one instance per connection:

- movement: per client tick, horizontal distance is bounded by the 1.8 client's
  own physics (last distance x friction + sprinting acceleration, the 0.2
  sprint-jump push on a jump), vertical rise by a jump (0.42 + Jump Boost), a
  ceiling, a step (0.6), or gravity in the air. Knockback the server sends,
  potions, liquids, ladders and slime are allowed for. A move outside the bound
  is set back to the last accepted position.
- ground: fall damage, critical hits and the jump statistic follow the ground
  the server sees under the player, not the client's onGround flag.
- timer: movement packets are counted against their arrival time; a client
  more than 250 ms ahead of real time has the extra moves set back.
- combat: an attack is dropped without the arm swing that precedes it, beyond
  one a tick, beyond 3.0 blocks (plus the hitbox border and the attacker's own
  last move) from every position the target held in the attacker's ping plus
  interpolation, or more than 60 degrees off the line of sight.

The bounds are tested against a model of the 1.8 client (onLivingUpdate,
moveEntityWithHeading, moveFlying, jump and moveEntity with its two-way
step-up) walking a world of floor, staggered slabs, ice, a low ceiling and
walls: 7.2 million honest ticks across six seeds raise nothing, and 1.3x speed,
flight, a 1-block step and a packet-criticals hop are caught. What the model
found and the bounds now allow: the client's onGround means collided going
down (so stepping off an edge is a ground tick, and a spawned client with zero
vertical motion is airborne on the floor), the vertical move happens over the
start before the sideways one, the step-up can cancel a jump (keeping its push)
or leave a landing floating on the ground, packets skip ticks under 0.03
blocks, and a box rebuilt from its centre overlaps the wall it touches.

pandaspigot.yml guard: enabled, enforce (false only logs), movement, timer,
combat, maxReach, log.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

